  "id": "DrugBank_DB09260 - MONDO_5279",
  "verbalization": "Parnaparin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Pulmonary Embolism (PE) through a series of interconnected indications. The evidence suggests that Parnaparin is associated with Purpura Fulminans, a severe form of purpura, which in turn is linked to Heparin, Bovine or Enoxaparin. These medications are known to have anticoagulant properties, which can increase the risk of thromboembolic events, including PE. The presence of Parnaparin in the indication chain for Purpura Fulminans, which is a condition characterized by disseminated intravascular coagulation, supports the hypothesis that Parnaparin may contribute to the development of PE through its anticoagulant effects. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Parnaparin could influence the risk of PE, although the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
